    "turn_text": "up. But for me, I didn't keep going to church because of a sense of religious obligation. I just felt like it made me a better person. And I was particularly inspired by the preacher at that college church. And his name was Peter J. Goes. And he talked a lot about the importance of service, about how it's not enough just to believe in service or support others who serve, you ought to find a way to go out and do something yourself to give back. And so, when I was approaching graduation, I looked at different options. I looked at the Peace Corps, I looked at teaching overseas, a lot of things that would have been a lot more popular with my parents. You can't escape all those men, mostly men, or just a few women on the wall of that church. And I think that suddenly being their age, for the first time in my life, I was their age. I saw their faces and the faces of my friends. very different than when you're growing up and these heroes from World War II were of a different",
