    "turn_text": "It was. In fact, we were sitting on the couch just glued to the television on September, I don't know, 13th or 14th, I think, following the attacks. And I remember I brought it up with them. I said, well, you know, tomorrow I'm going for my physical and, uh, Yeah, it was a very difficult, very difficult conversation to put it lightly. And sometimes I have students or, I mean, someone recently just, you know, who works on the Hill come up to me and just ask for advice, you know, hey, I'm thinking about going in and having a tough time explaining this to my parents, you know, do you have any advice? My advice is just plan on not being able to convince them. You know, mothers and fathers for literally thousands of years have not wanted to see their sons or daughters go to war. And you just have to recognize that you'll probably have to make this decision on your own.",
