    "turn_text": "Well, I mean, look, I mean, I'm certainly not speaking for all the troops. I would never pretend to do that. And I'm sure there's some troops that support him, but... But you want to have a commander in chief that you look up to. I remember that experience in the military. You want to have someone that even if you don't agree with, you can respect. I mean, I served under George W. Bush. I didn't vote for him twice. I didn't agree with his war. But I never thought that George W. Bush would collude with Russia, our greatest enemy.",
