  {
    "episode_id": 70869,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70869.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 103,
    "turn_text": "Look, the point is that you're not expected to agree with the politics of your commander-in-chief, but you ought to respect his or her integrity. You know, when I signed up for the Marines, I didn't know anything about military, go to Quantico for training. And one of the first things you learn is that you can drop out of a run and they'll give you another shot. You can fail a test and they'll let you retake it. But if you lie about anything, you're gone that afternoon. That's how fundamental integrity is in the military. And we have a commander-in-chief who lies many times a day. We have a commander-in-chief that we fundamentally can't trust.",
