    "turn_idx": 158,
    "turn_text": "they're doing things that are essential, they're important, and they're hard, and they're good paying jobs, by the way, too. But we don't seem to respect them very much. And we don't give people the opportunities to go to vocational school. I literally have lines out the door of the vocational schools in my district, and all Democrats seem to talk about is going to college. If you want to go to college, you should have the opportunity to go to college. But if you want to go to vocational school, you should have that opportunity as well and you should be respected for your job when you come out. And the irony of this situation is that when you actually look at how these jobs are changing and going away, it's actually much easier to to program a robot to program a computer, then it is to program a robot to fix an electrical cabinet. If we have some electrical problem in the building right now, you have to call an electrician. That's not going to be a robot for a long time, but literally computers are already programming themselves. We need to make sure that we're training people to be the machinists and electricians and plumbers that we still need.",
