    "turn_text": "Right. So anyway, that was 2014, and I spent my first two years just trying to do a good job as a congressman for my district. And I think I got named the most effective Democratic freshman or something like that. So we were just doing good work. We were just getting bills passed, working across the aisle, listening to constituents. But November 2016 was a wake-up call for me as it was for so many other Americans. And I woke up the next day. I was shocked, and like so many people across the country, I just started saying, you know, what can I do? How can I have an impact? And I decided that the best thing that we can do as Democrats is win back the House. I think that's the most realistic way we can put a check on President Trump, and I mean, it's extraordinary. I even hear Republicans, not just outside of Congress, but even a few in Congress saying, you know, the best thing for the country would be for Democrats to win control of the House. And so I said, let's focus on the house. Let's focus on veterans because they're sort of my niche and",
