    "turn_text": "what's the demarcation? You're absolutely right. So we have three criteria. Number one, they've got to be great servant leaders, people who are fundamentally doing this for the right reason. And that's a criteria that I don't think you see in many other organizations or many other lists of candidates. That's our most important criteria, great leaders. That's where we start. Number two, they've got to be in key races in winnable districts. You know, we're not going to just endorse an easy democratic seat. We're not going to endorse a a seat that's so deep red we don't have a prayer. And then the third thing is they've got to be the best general election candidate even in contested primaries. So this means that there are some extraordinary veterans out there that we haven't endorsed because they just don't meet, you know, they're not the best general election candidate",
