  {
    "episode_id": 70869,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70869.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 205,
    "turn_text": "Look, I've been very clear. I think it's time for a new generation of leadership in the party. And leader Pelosi has done extraordinary things. I mean, she's a master legislator in her own words. We wouldn't have Obamacare without her. And she should be respected for those things. But I think it's time to focus on the future. I think it's time to have a new generation of leaders stepping up. And there are extraordinary Democrats, both in Congress and coming into Congress, who represent that new generation, and I think can really take us forward. But again, it's- But that's what the party needs. It needs fresh faces. I",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
