    "turn_text": "mean, look, I'm not going to. I don't even remember the exact details of what would happen that particular day, but that certainly, you know, was an experience that we had as a platoon. And it really puts things into perspective. And the point is that after that experience of serving in the Marines and missing it more than I ever imagined, some people must listen to this and think, God, how can you miss being in a war? I miss those guys. I miss the commitment that we all had to our country. I miss the sense of purpose that we had every single day. And then you come back and you see a country that's just not living up to the values that we fought for, that we literally put our lives on the line for, that we believed so fundamentally that we were willing to risk everything to",
