  {
    "episode_id": 70869,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70869.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 253,
    "turn_text": "I think if you followed me around like literally 24 seven, you would be absolutely shocked about how little we talk about this like literally not at all. I mean, and maybe I'm just politically naive or maybe I'm not as calculating as I should be or something like that, but I'm just. still trying to serve my country. And if there's a different or better way to serve, then I'd be willing to look at that opportunity. But remember, I got here because I was literally living in Dallas, Texas, not planning to run at all and decided here's an opportunity to serve and I'm going to give it a shot. So I'm not coming at this with some long-term political plan or something like that. Is that like the morning after the election, the week after the election, you start thinking about that? I just think that, you know, I look at where I can have the biggest impact. I mean, I also didn't expect to be someone supporting all these extraordinary veterans running for Congress. We've endorsed, I think, 23 now, just of the core group of service veterans. We're now going to expand that even further. This is just a place where I saw that I could make a an impact, I could be a small part of being a change, and so I decided to step up and do it.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
